                <h2 class="section-title">What Is a Digital Signature Certificate?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Electronic equivalent of handwritten signature, legally valid under IT Act 2000. Issued by CCA-licensed Certifying Authorities. Contains: name, PAN, public key, serial number, validity, CA signature. Creates unique hash verifying identity + document integrity. For <a href="/income-tax-return">Income Tax Return</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>Since Jan 2021, only Class 3 DSCs issued (Class 2 merged). Sign Only for filing; Sign &amp; Encrypt for e-tendering. USB token or Paperless format. For <a href="/gst-registration/gurugram">GST Registration Gurugram</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for DSC:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>Class 3:</strong> Only class since Jan 2021 (Class 2 merged by CCA). All portals. 1/2/3-year validity</li><li><strong>Sign Only:</strong> For MCA V3, Income Tax, GST portal filings. Most common requirement</li><li><strong>Sign &amp; Encrypt:</strong> For e-tendering (GeM, CPPP). Also works for all other portals</li><li><strong>Paperless:</strong> Cloud-based. Any device. No physical token. Instant download. Recommended for travelers</li><li><strong>USB Token:</strong> Physical dongle. Single device. Best for desktop-only filing</li><li><strong>Video Verification:</strong> Aadhaar eKYC or video call. 5-10 min. Required by all CAs</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
